    <string name="tutorial_start">START</string>
    <string name="tutorial_step1_title">SHARE FROM AMAP</string>
    <string name="tutorial_step1_body">Open the AMap app, find a place (or long-press the map), tap Share and choose this app.

You can also copy the place in AMap and paste it here — multi-line text is fine.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_step2_title">CONFIGURE THE ALARM</string>
    <string name="tutorial_step2_body">Pick how far ahead you want to be alerted (100 m to 2 km, or a custom value), then choose the alert style:

· Notification only
· Notification + vibration
· Notification + vibration + alarm

One-shot alarms are deleted after alerting; repeating alarms fire on every entry.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_step3_title">GRANT PERMISSIONS</string>
    <string name="tutorial_step3_body">Precise location is required to register a geofence, and Android 10+ also needs “Allow all the time” so the alarm can fire while the app is in the background.

Notification permission is needed to show the alert.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_step4_title">WAIT FOR THE TRIGGER</string>
    <string name="tutorial_step4_body">The system geofence wakes the app up when you approach the target — no need to keep the app open, and no background GPS polling.

Response time is decided by the system and may be delayed by a minute or two.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_footer">You can replay this guide any time from Settings → Tutorial.</string>
